    "summary": "Acoustic Pigpen gems and a punchy second set with Turn On Your Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The July 12, 1970 Fillmore East show opens with a magical acoustic Pigpen set that includes Attics Of My Life and How Long Blues. The second set builds into a high‑energy stretch highlighted by It's A Man's World, Dancin' In The Street, Turn On Your Lovelight and a solid Uncle John’s Band encore. Recording quality is fair but the performance shines through.",
    "review": "On July 12 1970 at the Fillmore East the Dead delivered a night that feels like two shows in one. An intimate acoustic set led by Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan—featuring standout renditions of Attics Of My Life, How Long Blues and the soulful Tell It To Me—sets a relaxed tone before New Riders of the Purple Sage take the stage, giving Jerry Garcia a brief but memorable steel‑guitar spotlight. When the electric Dead return in the early morning hours they launch into a powerful second set: Easy Wind rolls into Mama Tried, then a soaring China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, followed by high‑octane performances of It's A Man's World, Dancin' In The Street and an exuberant Turn On Your Lovelight that carries the band to a rousing Uncle John’s Band encore. Though the best available tape is a fair‑quality audience recording with some muffled sections and occasional speed quirks, the energy and songcraft are unmistakable, making this a must‑listen for fans of the early‑70s acoustic‑electric blend.",
